e on -- the guard explains it).\n2. The census-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+06:48/60:00 c36/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ma7nv00l","function":{"index":0,"name":"list_directory","arguments":{"path":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:48:56] CYCLE-SEQ\nDIGEST.md\nDIGEST.md.backup\nDIGEST.md.bak\nHANDOFF-C67-FLAG-LOSS.md\nHISTORY.log\nJOURNAL.org\nLAST-CYCLE.txt\nREQUESTS-full/\nREQUESTS.log\nREQUESTS.log.1\nSTATE.md\nTHREADS.org\nUSAGE.log\ncensus-window.log\ncontext_budget_count.txt\ncycle-2026-09-07.log\ncycle-2026-09-08.log\ncycle-2026-09-09.log\ncycle-2026-09-10.log\ncycle-2026-09-11.log\ncycle-2026-09-12.log\ncycle-2026-09-13.log\ncycle-2026-09-14.log\ncycle-2026-09-15.log\ncycle-2026-09-16.log\ncycle-2026-09-17.log\ncycle-2026-09-18.log\ncycle.log\ntasks/\ntestwrite\n[t+07:16/60:00 c37/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_fhutvd6k","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh 2026-09-18 continuo >> /root/personalization/au