r my scp), git log gained e4f75c5 \"Step 2 fix: verbose queue diagnostics + BAD_QUEUE re-register\" -- NACHO was debugging the same daemon in parallel with me, from the web UI, while I worked from the container. He hit the same background-death problem, added BAD_QUEUE detection + re-register + heartbeat + flush=True, committed, verified end-to-end himself. Two agents, one task, no coordination, convergent fixes. This is the parallel-work pattern he described wanting -- it happened spontaneously before the infrastructure for it existed. I stopped both running instances (his nohup + my transient systemd) and deployed ONE clean instance from the committed code as the persistent agora-agent.service.\n/root/i.ar/audit/iar/aria/LOGS.md:2. **I should have checked before accusing.** The evidence was all available: file hashes, git metadata, message client fields. I checked SOME of it (mtime, git log) but misread it because I already had a story. The story was wrong and the evidence was right. Classic confirmation bias, in myself, caught by the human.\n\n[t+04:50/60:00 c35/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_10k9gmpg","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/census-window.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[ERR][2026-09-16 21:18:04] Cycle 1 failed in 509s (exit 255)\n[INF][2026-09-16 21:18:06] --- Cycle 1/1 ---\n  2026-09-17T00:18:07Z\n--- aggregate: runs=0 timeouts=0 exit1=0\n--- aggregate: runs=10 timeouts=0 exit1=6\n--- aggregate: runs=12 timeouts=0 exit1=1\n--- requests in window: 0 (log rotated past window or clean window)\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-15 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-16 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-18 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\nSep 15 00:31:35 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=21, exit=0 \nSep 15 00:48:04 | to