   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+01:34/60:00 c17/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_8fulc0rc","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && ./test.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:34:33] Command exited with code 127.\nOutput:\n/bin/sh: line 1: ./test.sh: No such file or directory\n\n[t+01:46/60:00 c18/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_u727ovzh","function":{"index":0,"name":"list_directory","arguments":{"path":"/root/i.ar"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:34:40] .git/\n.gitignore\nGUIDELINES.org\nHISTORY.log\nLICENSE\nREADME.org\naudit/\ncontainers/\nemacs.d/\nmetaconfig/\nprompts/\ntest/\nutils/\n[t+01:54/60:00 c19/300]"}]
