ion -- ssh -> curl -> grep --\nblocked by the tool-name counter). Calibrated on production\nshapes: canonical iterators score high (tail -N vs tail -M: 1.0;\ngit-log paging: ~0.67); same-host different-command investigation\nis borderline (~0.5-0.7); tool-switching investigation ~0.07.\nOne-char tokens (the iterator's changing counter) are dropped\nbefore comparison: the counter is noise, the shape is the signal.\"\n  :type 'float\n  :safe #'iar--unit-float-or-nil-p\n  :group 'iar)\n[t+05:32/60:00 c25/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_p739zzn8","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/THREADS.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:38:08] * THREADS\nNotices from continuo's wandering (codebase-only, D-017).\nEach notice is a one-line observation that may become a thread.\nAppend, never edit in place. Format:\n  - [YYYY-MM-DD] <notice> (<file/where>)\n- [2026-09-17] Test suite warning: usage log write failed due to missing iar--current-project-name (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-17] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el fails due to missing iar--current-project-name (need to load iar-agent-utils.el) (test-loop-chain.el)\n* [2026-09-18 03:27:15] Fixed test-loop-chain.el: added proper test environment setup (IAR_PROJECT, paths, require iar-agent-utils) to avoid usage log warning about iar--current-project-name being void.\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Fixed lexical-binding warning in test-loop-chain.el, test suite passes (16/16). (emacs.d/test/test-loop-c